                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Despite the game reporting a ping of 60, the game plays like I'm running a ping of 1200- that is to say, the game is unplayable. Whatever the heck is wrong with this game's servers is hindering what appears to be a reasonably functional, albeit over-simple, sports mini-game. Think air hockey with MOBA powers, and you've pretty much got the game nailed. There's a single game mode, and a small handful of different powered MOBA-style heroes to play with, meaning you'll experience all the game has to offer within about 15 minutes of play.\n\nIf the servers get fixed, this game'd warrant a recommendation, at least under the consideration that would-be-owners understand the game is very simplistic and very tied to MOBA mechanics. While value is a relative thing, I imagine most would find this game (once fixed) to warrant a retail price of about $6, so it may be worth waiting for this game to leave Early Acc- :looks at the game page: Uhm. Well, anyway- it may be worth waiting to see if the game improves enough to warrant its price, or if it'll at least fix its server problems and drop its price to match its shallowness of content.\n\nIn the meantime, free key promotions for the game have left quite a few spare copies floating around the internet, so you may be able to pick up this game for just about nothing regardless.",
